@@ -57 +57 @@ chaosx.help.body.events: "§YLive Values§!\nEvents fired: §Y[?global.total_eve
-chaosx.help.body.chaos_meter: "§YLive Values§!\nChaos: [GetChaosMeterValueColored]  Tier: §Y[GetChaosTierName]§!\nTimer modifier: §Y[?global.chaos_timer_modifier|.2]x§!\nRecorded deaths: §Y[GetChaosMeterDeathsTotalDisplay]§!\nAir contamination: [GetAirContaminationValueColored]\n\n§YChaos Meter§!\nThe global Chaos Meter shortens event timing, unlocks stronger escalation, and increases eligible cluster pressure as its tier rises.\n\n§YDeaths System§!\nMilitary casualties and state-linked civilian deaths from war, disasters, disease, famine, forced displacement, camps, and unconventional weapons enter one shared ledger. Civilian entries remove real state population, and each source can convert its recorded toll into chaos.\n\n§YAir Cleanliness§!\nAir Cleanliness tracks atmospheric contamination from chemical hazards, outbreaks, fallout, smoke, ash, and aerosols. Thresholds at 25%, 50%, 75%, and 100% accelerate outbreaks, worsen Air Winter, activate the Air Cleanliness Treaty, and can enable the Fallout consequence. Its Chaos Meter tab shows recovery and a permanent source ledger.\n\n§YFamine Mechanics§!\nFamine tracks Food Security, Food Reserves, and Relief Access in each affected state. Conditions progress through stable, supply strain, acute shortage, famine, and catastrophic famine. Relief, route, reserve, import, airlift, and evacuation actions can reverse pressure, while severe mortality enters the Deaths System and may create a separate migration request.\n\n§YMigration Mechanics§!\nMigration tracks Displacement Load, Reception Capacity, and Border Policy as cohorts move through flight, reception, settlement, resettlement, and return. Population moves between proven origins and destinations; unsafe routes or violent pushback can add deaths. Decisions, missions, reports, and the migration mapmode manage corridors and outcomes.\n\n§YCamp System Mechanics§!\nThe Repression and Camps System covers detention, forced labor, gulags, experiment programs, discovery, reform, and dismantlement. Active sites remove real population through the Deaths System and store responsibility and evidence for later Condemnation. Country routes and its five tabs show territories, active sites, programs, discovery, and reform without revealing hidden evidence early."
+chaosx.help.body.chaos_meter: "§YLive Values§!\nChaos: [GetChaosMeterValueColored]  Tier: §Y[GetChaosTierName]§!\nTimer modifier: §Y[?global.chaos_timer_modifier|.2]x§!\nRecorded deaths: §Y[GetChaosMeterDeathsTotalDisplay]§!\nAir contamination: [GetAirContaminationValueColored]\n\n§YChaos Meter§!\nThe global Chaos Meter shortens event timing, unlocks stronger escalation, and increases eligible cluster pressure as its tier rises.\n\n§YDeaths System§!\nMilitary casualties and state-linked civilian deaths from war, disasters, disease, famine, forced displacement, camps, and unconventional weapons enter one shared ledger. Civilian entries remove real state population, and each source can convert its recorded toll into chaos.\n\n§YAir Cleanliness§!\nAir Cleanliness tracks atmospheric contamination from chemical hazards, outbreaks, fallout, smoke, ash, and aerosols. Thresholds at 25%, 50%, 75%, and 100% accelerate outbreaks, worsen Air Winter, activate the Air Cleanliness Treaty, and can enable the Fallout consequence. Its Chaos Meter tab shows recovery and a permanent source ledger.\n\n§YFamine Mechanics§!\nFood shortages become a crisis when war, disasters, or disrupted supplies leave people without enough to eat. Hunger can kill civilians and drive survivors from affected regions. Relief supplies, restored transport, imports, and evacuation can protect your population and help the country recover.\n\n§YMigration Mechanics§!\nMigration affects your country when people flee war, persecution, hunger, or disasters, or when you receive those fleeing elsewhere. Flight reduces the population of affected regions, while arrivals can overwhelm local support. Border policies, safe routes, relief, settlement, and return decisions shape where people can live and whether they survive the journey.\n\n§YCamp System Mechanics§!\nCamps become relevant where your government uses detention or forced labor, including in occupied territory. Camps can cause civilian deaths and suffering, while exposed abuses can bring condemnation against those responsible. Reform and dismantlement decisions let you curb abuses or close the camps."
